  "salt": "OfGJJO6p20SAqDGY-tLuIA==",
  "text": "Romano-Celtic is a term from archaeology. It names the gods and faith of the mainland Celts and of Britain as seen in works of art from the years after Rome took the land. The Celts rarely drew their gods in human shape. A few early images show divine beings with the bodies of animals. Most of the gods were drawn as plain signs or symbols, so the gods are hard to read.",
